    {
      "source": "News On AIR",
      "title": "5 hours ago | International 359 PM Narendra Modi and US Vice-Prez JD Vance discuss ways to further strengthen Comprehensive Globa... Prime Minister Narendra Modi received a phone call from US Vice President JD Vance yesterday. In a social media post, Mr Modi said they discussed ways to further deepen the India-US Comprehensive Global Strategic Partnership across key areas. They noted the sustained momentum in the high-level engagements and reaffirmed their commitment to further strengthening cooperation in trade, defence, critical and emerging technologies, energy security and critical minerals. Both leaders also exchanged vi...",
      "url": "https://newsonair.gov.in/pm-narendra-modi-receives-phone-call-from-us-vice-president-jd-vance/",
      "date": "",
      "content": "News On AIR | August 9, 2026 8:36 AM Prime Minister Narendra Modi received a phone call from US Vice President JD Vance yesterday. In a social media post, Mr Modi said they discussed ways to further deepen the India-US Comprehensive Global Strategic Partnership across key areas. They noted the sustained momentum in the high-level engagements and reaffirmed their commitment to further strengthening cooperation in trade, defence, critical and emerging technologies, energy security and critical minerals. Both leaders also exchanged views on regional and global developments of mutual interest. Mr Modi congratulated Mr Vance and the Second Lady, Usha, on the birth of their son and conveyed best wishes to the entire family. Privacy Policy | Copyright © 2026 News On Air. All rights reserved",
      "content_chars": 794,
      "type": "News On AIR"
    },
    {
      "source": "News On AIR",
      "title": "5 hours ago | National 230 Har Ghar Tiranga campaign begins today, coinciding with 150th anniversary of India’s National Son...",
      "url": "https://newsonair.gov.in/har-ghar-tiranga-campaign-begins-today/",
      "date": "",
      "content": "News On AIR | August 9, 2026 8:32 AM The Har Ghar Tiranga campaign will begin today and will run through 17th August. The initiative is aimed at encouraging citizens to hoist the National Flag and participate in activities celebrating patriotism, national unity and India’s cultural heritage. The campaign, which began in 2022 as part of the Azadi Ka Amrit Mahotsav celebrations, has since evolved into one of the country’s largest public participation movements. Over the years, it has emerged a true people’s movement that inspires citizens across regions and communities to celebrate the Tricolour as a symbol of India’s unity, honour and collective national identity. This year’s campaign holds special significance as it coincides with the 150th anniversary of India’s National Song, “Vande Mataram”, bringing together the National Flag and the National Song in a unique celebration of patriotism. As part of the celebrations, mass singing of Vande Mataram will be organised across the country. As part of the Independence Day commemorations, the Government will also observe Partition Horrors Remembrance Day on August 14 across the country to remember the suffering and displacement caused by the Partition of India. The observance will include silent marches, exhibitions on Partition, documentary screenings and other commemorative programmes across States and Union Territories. Inviting citizens to participate in the campaign, the Union Culture Ministry urged people to hoist the National Flag with pride, learn and sing Vande Mataram, take part in community activities and join the nation in remembering the sacrifices that shaped India’s journey to Independence. More than 200 Indian Embassies, High Commissions and Consulates will organise a series of events to mark the campaign. A key highlight this year will be the Surya Path Tiranga digital relay, in which 54 Indian Missions and Posts, selected according to the sunrise sequence across time zones, will participate. The relay will begin on 15th August from India’s easternmost diplomatic mission in Fiji and conclude at the Consulate General of India in San Francisco. Privacy Policy | Copyright © 2026 News On Air. All rights reserved",
      "content_chars": 2206,
      "type": "News On AIR"
    },
    {
      "source": "News On AIR",
      "title": "5 hours ago | National 212 Amarnath Yatra to remain suspended from both Pahalgam and Baltal routes",
      "url": "https://newsonair.gov.in/amarnath-yatra-to-remain-suspended-over-next-few-days/",
      "date": "",
      "content": "News On AIR | August 9, 2026 8:20 AM In Jammu and Kashmir, the annual Amarnath Yatra will remain suspended on both the Pahalgam and Baltal routes from today due to recent rains, repair work of pilgrimage tracks and the forecast of adverse weather conditions over the next few days. The decision to temporarily halt the yatra has been taken keeping in view the condition of the tracks as well as the weather forecast issued by the India Meteorological Department. No fresh Yatra convoy was allowed to leave the Bhagwati Nagar base camp in Jammu yesterday as a precautionary measure amid rains and inclement weather conditions prevailing in Ramban district and parts of Kashmir. Meanwhile, the 28th batch, comprising 1,202 pilgrims who had completed darshan at the Holy Cave and were staying at the Baltal base camp, was allowed to proceed towards Jammu in a convoy of 44 vehicles. The returning pilgrims included 867 males, 251 females, one child, 79 sadhus and four sadhvis. The convoy comprised 28 heavy vehicles, one medium motor vehicle, 11 light motor vehicles and four trucks. 3336 pilgrims performed darshan at the Holy Cave yesterday. The pilgrims included 2384 males, 569 females, 21 children, 20 sadhus, six sadhvis, four transgender pilgrims and 332 security personnel. With this, the total number of pilgrims who have performed darshan during the 2026 Yatra has reached 4 lakh 80 thousand and 19. The 57-day-long Amarnath Yatra commenced on July 3 simultaneously from both the traditional Chandanwari route in Anantnag district and the Baltal route in Ganderbal district and is scheduled to culminate with the traditional Chadi Mubarak ceremony on August 28. However, due to the recent rains, a necessity for the repair and maintenance of the Yatra tracks at vulnerable stretches has been felt, which is being undertaken by the Border Roads Organisation (BRO). The IMD has predicted adverse weather conditions over the next few days. Hence, the Yatra shall remain suspended from both routes with effect from today. Authorities have appealed to pilgrims to follow advisories issued by the competent authorities from time to time in the interest of their safety and the smooth conduct of the pilgrimage. Privacy Policy | Copyright © 2026 News On Air. All rights reserved",
      "content_chars": 2279,
      "type": "News On AIR"
    },
    {
      "source": "News On AIR",
      "title": "5 hours ago | Sports 96 Sagnik-Sayantan win Gold medal in Under-31 Pairs at 9th World Bridge Federation Youth Transnation...",
      "url": "https://newsonair.gov.in/sagnik-roy-and-sayantan-kushari-win-gold-medal-in-under-31-pairs-at-9th-world-bridge-federation-youth-transnational-championships/",
      "date": "",
      "content": "News On AIR | August 9, 2026 8:35 AM Sagnik Roy and Sayantan Kushari won the gold medal in the Under-31 Pairs at the 9th World Youth Transnational Championships in Hefei, China, yesterday. In the first elimination round, 34 pairs competed and the top 14 advanced to Flight A, including the Indian duo. They then competed in a round-robin format, with Sagnik and Sayantan finishing on top with 377.67 match points. M Fereneca and F Katusich of Croatia finished second with 357.78 match points, while China’s J Han and Z Wang took the third spot with 335.92 match points. Privacy Policy | Copyright © 2026 News On Air. All rights reserved",
      "content_chars": 636,
      "type": "News On AIR"
    },
    {
      "source": "News On AIR",
      "title": "NBA disburses over 3 crore rupees under Access and Benefit Sharing mechanism to 33 States/UTs and National Institutes",
      "url": "https://newsonair.gov.in/nba-disburses-over-3-crore-rupees-under-access-and-benefit-sharing-mechanism-to-33-states-uts-and-national-institutes/",
      "date": "",
      "content": "News On AIR | August 9, 2026 1:21 PM The National Biodiversity Authority (NBA) has disbursed over 3 crore rupees as Access and Benefit Sharing (ABS) to 33 State Biodiversity Boards, Union Territory Biodiversity Councils and National Institutes. The Ministry of Environment, Forest and Climate Change said that the release covers a diverse range of India’s agrobiodiversity, including tomato, chilli, brinjal and deep-frozen Sahiwal cattle semen. It informed that cumulative ABS disbursements by the NBA have now exceeded 166 crore rupees. The Ministry also said that each release further strengthens the link between biodiversity conservation, scientific research and the livelihoods of the communities that conserve India’s rich biological resources. Privacy Policy | Copyright © 2026 News On Air. All rights reserved",
      "content_chars": 818,
      "type": "News On AIR"
    },
    {
      "source": "News On AIR",
      "title": "NIA arrests another accused in connection with seizure of huge consignment of illegal explosives in Malappuram",
      "url": "https://newsonair.gov.in/nia-arrests-another-accused-in-connection-with-seizure-of-huge-consignment-of-illegal-explosives-in-malappuram/",
      "date": "",
      "content": "News On AIR | August 9, 2026 1:00 PM The National Investigation Agency (NIA) has arrested another accused in connection with the seizure of a huge consignment of illegal explosives in Malappuram, Keralam. The Agency informed that the accused was arrested yesterday from Manjeri in the Malappuram district. NIA said that the accused is a main conspirator and was involved in the illegal procurement of the explosives seized in the case. The latest arrest comes a day after the NIA arrested three more accused from Vijayapura in Karnataka on Friday, taking the total number of arrests in the case to ten. The case relates to the seizure of 89,600 explosive sticks and 10,500 shock tubes from a lorry parked in the compound of Farha Hollow Bricks Company on the Chemmad-Thalappara Road in Malappuram. NIA further said that investigation into the larger conspiracy and the illegal procurement and movement of the explosives is continuing. Privacy Policy | Copyright © 2026 News On Air. All rights reserved",
      "content_chars": 1001,
      "type": "News On AIR"
    },
    {
      "source": "News On AIR",
      "title": "Vice President CP Radhakrishnan pays tribute to freedom fighters of Quit India Movement",
      "url": "https://newsonair.gov.in/vice-president-cp-radhakrishnan-pays-tribute-to-freedom-fighters-of-quit-india-movement/",
      "date": "",
      "content": "News On AIR | August 9, 2026 11:04 AM Vice President CP Radhakrishnan has paid tributes to the freedom fighters who participated in the Quit India Movement. In a social media post, he said that they united the nation in the struggle for freedom, taking inspiration from Mahatma Gandhi’s clarion call of Do or Die. The Vice President added that their courage, sacrifice and patriotism continue to inspire generations. Privacy Policy | Copyright © 2026 News On Air. All rights reserved",
