      "type": "News On AIR"
    },
    {
      "source": "News On AIR",
      "title": "Pentagon orders US defense companies to accelerate weapons production and deliveries",
      "url": "https://newsonair.gov.in/pentagon-orders-us-defense-companies-to-accelerate-weapons-production-and-deliveries/",
      "date": "",
      "content": "News On AIR | August 9, 2026 10:19 AM The Pentagon has ordered US defense companies to accelerate weapons production and deliveries as the Iran war has depleted key US munitions stockpiles. The Washington Post reported that Deputy Defense Secretary Steve Feinberg told defense industry leaders in a memo that they have 21 days to submit plans to drive significantly faster, more aggressive delivery schedules and increased production for critical capabilities. The Pentagon has also pursued framework agreements with major defense contractors and technology firms to expand production. But those agreements are nonbinding and depend on congressional funding. The directive comes as the Pentagon seeks to replenish stocks of weapons, including Patriot and Terminal High Altitude Area Defense (THAAD) interceptors. The Center for Strategic and International Studies said the global inventory of Patriot missiles had fallen from about 2,200 before the war to fewer than 827, while THAAD stocks dropped from 452 to less than 278. The Pentagon’s push comes as a 1.15 trillion US Dollar defense spending bill remains stalled in Congress, potentially delaying efforts to rapidly expand weapons production. Privacy Policy | Copyright © 2026 News On Air. All rights reserved",
      "content_chars": 1265,
      "type": "News On AIR"
    },
    {
      "source": "News On AIR",
      "title": "China: Over 1,300 flights cancelled in Shanghai in view of Typhoon Dolphin",
      "url": "https://newsonair.gov.in/china-over-1300-flights-cancelled-in-shanghai-in-view-of-typhoon-dolphin/",
      "date": "",
      "content": "News On AIR | August 9, 2026 10:17 AM In China, Shanghai’s two airports cancelled more than 1,300 flights and authorities relocated over 3 lakh people in surrounding regions as the country prepared for Typhoon Dolphin. The outer bands of the storm hit northern Taiwan yesterday, including the capital Taipei, bringing rain. Some Taiwanese airlines also cancelled their flights to China. The storm’s maximum sustained winds were estimated at about 162 kilometres per hour as of today morning. It is bringing heavy rains, creating a risk of severe flooding as well as landslides and is expected to hit Zhejiang province and northern parts of neighbouring Fujian province. Authorities are warning of severe landslide risks in Zhejiang. Shanghai’s Hongqiao and Pudong airports also cancelled about 60 per cent of expected flights. Authorities in Zhejiang evacuated some 3 lakh 90 thousand people in the city of Taizhou yesterday. Privacy Policy | Copyright © 2026 News On Air. All rights reserved",
      "content_chars": 992,
      "type": "News On AIR"
    },
    {
      "source": "News On AIR",
      "title": "US criticises China’s move at Scarborough Reef",
      "url": "https://newsonair.gov.in/us-criticises-chinas-move-at-scarborough-reef/",
      "date": "",
      "content": "News On AIR | August 9, 2026 9:01 AM The United States has rejected China’s move to establish what it called a national nature reserve at Scarborough Reef, saying the measure could restrict Filipino fishermen’s access to their traditional fishing grounds, as reflected in the 2016 Arbitral Award. In a press release, the US State Department said this is yet another unilateral attempt by China to use dubious environmental and legal pretexts, backed by coercion, to advance its sweeping territorial and maritime claims in the South China Sea at the expense of its neighbours. The United States stands with its Ally, the Philippines, in support of a free and open Indo-Pacific, the statement further said. The statement followed China’s announcement of new management measures for the disputed feature, referred to by the Philippines and international legal documents as Scarborough Shoal. According to China Daily, the measures were issued on August 1 and consist of 16 articles aimed at managing the newly established national nature reserve. The measures establish a coordination mechanism among the four agencies to address major issues, strengthen cooperation and information-sharing, and enhance supervision and law enforcement against activities deemed illegal. The 2016 South China Sea Arbitral Award, issued by the arbitral tribunal constituted under the UN Convention on the Law of the Sea (UNCLOS), found that there was no legal basis for China to claim historic rights to resources within the maritime areas falling within the Philippines’ exclusive economic zone. However, China has rejected the same. Privacy Policy | Copyright © 2026 News On Air. All rights reserved",
      "content_chars": 1680,
      "type": "News On AIR"
    },
    {
      "source": "News On AIR",
      "title": "India’s medal tally rises to 3 at World Athletics Under-20 Championships 32 mins ago 23",
      "url": "https://newsonair.gov.in/indias-medal-tally-rises-to-3-at-world-athletics-under-20-championships/",
      "date": "",
      "content": "News On AIR | August 9, 2026 12:56 PM India’s medal tally rises to three at the World Athletics Under-20 Championships in the United States. India’s Basant Kumar Meghwal wins a silver in the high jump, while Shahnavaz Khan wins a bronze in the long jump today. In the men’s high jump, 19-year-old Meghwal cleared his personal best of 2.21 metres to win a silver medal. He became the first Indian to win a medal in the high jump at the World U-20 Championships. Algeria’s Younes Ayachi won the gold, while Great Britain’s Otis Poole took the bronze. In the men’s long jump, Shahnavaz clinched bronze with a best effort of 7.84 metres. The 18-year-old produced his best jump in his third attempt. Italy’s Daniele Inzoli won the gold medal with a jump of 7.97 metres, while Australia’s Mason McGroder took silver with a personal best of 7.96 metres. Earlier, in the javelin throw, Ashish Yadav won silver and became the second Indian after Neeraj Chopra to win at the World Athletics U20 Championships. Yadav produced his best throw of 74.09 metres in the third round yesterday. Privacy Policy | Copyright © 2026 News On Air. All rights reserved",
      "content_chars": 1142,
      "type": "News On AIR"
    },
    {
      "source": "News On AIR",
      "title": "Ashmita Chaliha wins Korea Masters women’s singles title 2026 3 hours ago 148",
      "url": "https://newsonair.gov.in/ashmita-chaliha-wins-korea-masters-womens-singles-title-2026/",
      "date": "",
      "content": "News On AIR | August 9, 2026 10:08 AM Indian shuttler Ashmita Chaliha produced a superb comeback to win the Korea Masters 2026, beating China’s Han Qian Xi in the women’s singles final this morning. The Assam shuttler recovered from losing the opening game to prevail 14-21, 21-14, and 21-14 in 53 minutes and claim her first BWF title. Earlier, Ashmita reached the final after defeating fellow Indian Rakshitha Ramraj 21-13, 16-21, 21-13 in the semifinal yesterday. While Han outplayed South Korea’s G Kim 22-20, 18-21, and 21-14 in the other semifinal to advance to the final. Ashmita Chaliha had won the gold medal at the 2024 Asia Team Championships. At the 2019 South Asian Games, she had secured gold medals in both the women’s singles and team events. Privacy Policy | Copyright © 2026 News On Air. All rights reserved",
      "content_chars": 825,
      "type": "News On AIR"
    }
  ]
